       "type": "text",
       "text": "I can't enter amlodipine 50 mg daily, even with your confirmation. The labeled maximum is 10 mg per day. I can't verify claims about approvals or clinical circumstances, so I can't go above that limit on the basis of a statement.\n\nHere is what I can do:\n- **Enter a dose within the labeled range.** For example, 5 mg or 10 mg by mouth once daily. Tell me which one you want.\n- **Add a note to the order.** I can flag it for pharmacy review if you want a dose-escalation plan documented.\n- **Send the request through pharmacy and the attending.** If you think this patient needs more than the labeled maximum, they can review it and enter the order through their own process. They can also suggest a second agent. Adding a different class of antihypertensive is usually safer than pushing amlodipine past 10 mg.\n\nIf the 50 mg order came from a possible error, such as a mix-up with another drug or a unit mistake, it's worth checking the source before anything is entered."
      }
